<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>Alignment - 标签 - lilfry's library</title><link>https://lilfry09.github.io/tags/alignment/</link><description>Alignment - 标签 - lilfry's library</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>zh-CN</language><managingEditor>lilfry@sjtu.edu.cn (lilfry)</managingEditor><webMaster>lilfry@sjtu.edu.cn (lilfry)</webMaster><copyright>All rights reserved.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Wed, 08 Apr 2026 14:20:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://lilfry09.github.io/tags/alignment/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>面试高频：Bradley-Terry vs Plackett-Luce，奖励建模到底差在哪</title><link>https://lilfry09.github.io/ai/bt-vs-pl-ranking-in-alignment/</link><pubDate>Wed, 08 Apr 2026 14:20:00 +0800</pubDate><author>fry</author><guid>https://lilfry09.github.io/ai/bt-vs-pl-ranking-in-alignment/</guid><description><![CDATA[<p>在 MSRA 这类偏研究工程结合的面试里，如果话题进入 <code>Alignment</code> 和 <code>Reward Modeling</code>，面试官很喜欢用 <code>Bradley-Terry (BT)</code> 和 <code>Plackett-Luce (PL)</code> 来看你对排序学习底层原理的掌握深度。</p>
<p>一句话先定锚：</p>
<p><strong>BT 模型是 PL 模型在候选集大小 N=2 时的特例。</strong></p>
<p>如果你是从 PyTorch 直觉出发，可以粗糙理解成：</p>
<ul>
<li>BT 更像“二分类的 Sigmoid”</li>
<li>PL 更像“列表级的序列 Softmax”</li>
</ul>
<p>它们都在做同一件事：把人类主观偏好，映射成连续的奖励分数。</p>]]></description></item></channel></rss>